        "original_id": "731ad065-874d-5fd8-adcb-d5e1581e1dd7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Florida, Lake Okeechobee, Miami River, downtown Miami, Clifton, Passaic, Passaic County, New Jersey\n- Systems: Miami Canal, C-6 Canal, Dundee Canal\n- Concepts: industrial canals, hydropower, manufacturing\n\nFacts:\n- The Miami Canal, also called the C-6 Canal, flows in Florida from Lake Okeechobee to its terminus at the Miami River.\n- The Miami River flows through downtown Miami.\n- The Dundee Canal was an industrial canal in Clifton and Passaic in Passaic County, New Jersey.\n- The Dundee Canal supplied hydropower and water for manufacturing.",
